.\" sliver-settings(1). Prose: docs/user-guide.md, docs/ux.md.
.TH SLIVER\-SETTINGS 1 2026-10-13 "sliver 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sliver\-settings \- edit the Touch Bar layout, rules and appearance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sliver\-settings
.RI [ preset.sliver ...]
.br
.B sliver\-settings
.BR \-\-version " | " \-V
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sliver\-settings
is the graphical editor for Sliver, a GTK4/libadwaita app.
Everything it changes is written to your configuration file
.RB ( sliver\-config (5)),
keeping your comments and formatting, and the running
.BR sliver\-agent (1)
picks it up at once.
Hand edits and the app can be mixed freely: when the file changes on disk, the window reloads it.
.PP
On first launch, when you have no configuration yet, it explains the safe hatch (press Fn twice and
hold it to get Escape and F1\(enF12, whatever the layout says) and offers a starting point.
.PP
Given
.I preset.sliver
files (or when a file manager opens one), it shows each preset for review: the layout, and every
script and command it would run, before anything is imported.
.SH PAGES
.TP
.B Bar
A live preview of any layer (base, Fn, custom layers), as it would look in a chosen context.
Drag modules from the library onto the preview, drag to reorder, drag off to remove, and drag the
width handle to resize.
The inspector edits the selected module: its content, style and actions.
.B Mirror
also shows the layout you're editing on the real Touch Bar while the window is focused.
.TP
.B Layouts & Rules
Which layout shows when: per app, workspace and state (media playing, screen locked, on battery,
\&...).
The rule winning right now is marked
.BR "Active now" ,
with the reason.
.TP
.B Gestures
When taps fire (on touch or on lift), how the Fn key works (hold or toggle), and what
whole\-bar gestures (swipes) do.
.TP
.B Appearance
Theme, stylesheet, fonts, corner radius, outlines, accent colour, animations and press feedback.
.TP
.B Display & Power
Brightness (adaptive or fixed, with a curve editor), dim and off timeouts, the on\-battery profile,
and pixel shift.
.TP
.B Apps
Which apps and scripts may put items on the bar through the D\-Bus API.
.TP
.B Profiles & Presets
Switch, create and delete profiles (whole configurations), and export or import presets.
.TP
.B Status
Which configuration file is in use and whether it loads, the files being watched, hardware facts
(physical Escape key or not, the safe hatch), and configuration problems.
.SH BANNERS
Across the top of the window:
.B sliver\-agent isn't running
(with
.BR Start ),
an invalid configuration (with a way to open the file), and a layout that leaves the F\-keys
reachable only through the safe hatch (with
.BR "Add F\-keys back" ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z
Undo the last change.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+Shift+Z ", " Ctrl+Y
Redo.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sliver/sliver.toml
The configuration it edits
.RI ( $XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is honoured).
.TP
.I ~/.config/sliver/profiles/
Named profiles.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sliver\-config (5),
.BR sliver\-stylesheet (5),
.BR sliverctl (1),
.BR sliver\-agent (1),
.BR sliverd (8)
.PP
.I docs/user\-guide.md
in the sliver sources.
